# 👻 Ghost Homelab Architecture

### Triple NAT Topology with Hardware Security Checkpoint and Zero-Subscription AI Stack

> **Concepts document — part of the ScryptGate research framework**  
> *A reproducible reference architecture for a fully self-hosted, layered-encrypted,  
> ghost network with hardware-rooted AI agent security. Zero ongoing subscriptions.*

-----

## Overview

This document describes a complete homelab network architecture built around three core properties:

1. **Ghost topology** — Labs infrastructure is physically invisible to the internet and logically invisible to the home network. Three NAT layers with a mandatory software kill switch.
2. **Hardware security checkpoint** — A repurposed cryptographic ASIC (see [ScryptGate](../README.md)) sits between the network edge and the AI inference stack. No automated action executes without hardware-verified proof-of-work.
3. **Zero subscriptions** — Every component is self-hosted and free. WireGuard replaces commercial VPN. DuckDNS + Let’s Encrypt replaces paid TLS. Podman replaces Docker Desktop. Grafana + Prometheus replaces commercial monitoring.

This architecture runs on consumer hardware available secondhand for under $500 total.

