## Hardware Requirements

This architecture is deliberately hardware-agnostic. Any devices filling these roles work. The reference implementation used consumer hardware under $500 total secondhand.

### Role Requirements

|Role         |Minimum Requirements                                  |Reference Implementation       |
|-------------|------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|
|Edge Router  |OpenWrt or DD-WRT/Merlin capable, WireGuard support   |ASUS GT-AX6000 (Merlin)        |
|Middle Buffer|OpenWrt capable, Wi-Fi, 64MB+ RAM                     |Netgear R6120 (OpenWrt 25.12.1)|
|Server       |Dual NIC or Wi-Fi + Ethernet, 8GB+ RAM, Linux         |MSI laptop, Fedora Server, LUKS|
|Workstation  |16GB+ RAM for Qubes, IOMMU support for GPU passthrough|Desktop, Qubes OS              |
|ScryptGate   |Any Scrypt ASIC with hackable controller              |Goldshell MiniDOGE 1           |
|Switch       |Any unmanaged switch                                  |Any brand                      |

### Why This Specific Topology

```
Edge Router (NAT #1)
    → Handles public internet exposure
    → Only device with a public IP
    → WireGuard endpoint for remote access
    → Home network lives here — isolated from everything below

Middle Buffer (NAT #2)
    → Adds a dedicated routing hop between edge and server
    → Even if edge router is compromised, attacker hits this next
    → Runs the lightweight security agent (low RAM requirement)
    → Wi-Fi uplink to server = no physical port needed on server

Server (NAT #3 / routing)
    → The intelligence layer
    → Routes Labs traffic — mandatory choke point
    → All AI inference and agent logic lives here
    → Kill switch is here — if server is off, Labs are dark

Labs (behind server)
    → Complete darkness from internet perspective
    → Can only reach internet through server
    → Server can log, inspect, or kill all their traffic
```

Every layer has exactly one job. No layer does two jobs.

