## Encryption Layer Map

Every hop uses a different algorithm. No two adjacent layers share the same cryptographic primitive.

|Hop              |Protocol       |Algorithm              |Where                         |
|-----------------|---------------|-----------------------|------------------------------|
|Wi-Fi uplink     |WPA3-SAE       |AES-256-CCMP           |Server ↔ Middle router        |
|Remote VPN       |WireGuard      |ChaCha20-Poly1305      |Anywhere → Edge router        |
|Public web       |TLS 1.3 (Caddy)|ECDHE-AES-256-GCM      |Internet → Server             |
|Internal services|mTLS           |ECDHE-ChaCha20-Poly1305|Container ↔ container         |
|Agent signing    |NaCl/libsodium |Ed25519                |Middle router → Approval API  |
|ScryptGate PoW   |Scrypt         |N=1048576, r=8, p=1    |All agent requests            |
|SSH everywhere   |OpenSSH        |Ed25519-AES-256-CTR    |All management                |
|Disk volumes     |LUKS2          |AES-XTS-256            |Server sensitive data         |
|Backups          |rclone crypt   |AES-256-CTR            |Server → local encrypted drive|
|Qubes inter-VM   |Xen hypervisor |AES-128-GCM            |Workstation VM isolation      |

No single algorithm compromise breaks more than one layer.

