## ScryptGate Integration

The ScryptGate hardware checkpoint sits on `YOUR_MIDDLE_SUBNET` alongside the server’s uplink interface.

```
Middle router agent detects anomaly
    ↓
Generates proposal with Scrypt PoW token
    ↓
POST to server approval API
    ↓
Server calls ScryptGate /verify/pow before queuing
    ↓
ASIC verifies at hardware speed
    ↓
Valid → enters human review queue
Invalid → rejected, logged, alert sent
    ↓
Human approves via HTTPS UI (WireGuard access only)
    ↓
Admin signs approval with Ed25519 key from vault
    ↓
Middle router agent executes — logs result
```

For full ScryptGate documentation see the [project README](../README.md).

