## Security Properties

### What This Architecture Guarantees

```
1. No inbound path to Labs exists
   → Triple NAT with no port forwards to Labs
   → Verified by external port scan

2. Home network has zero visibility into Labs
   → Different subnets with no advertised routes
   → Verified by ping test from home devices

3. Labs go dark if server goes offline
   → Kill switch is structural — not a rule
   → Verified by taking server offline

4. All agent actions require hardware verification
   → ScryptGate PoW on every proposal
   → Fails closed if ASIC unreachable

5. All agent actions require human approval
   → No automated execution without admin signature
   → Admin key lives in air-gapped vault

6. All sensitive data is encrypted at rest
   → LUKS2 on server volumes
   → Passphrase required on every boot

7. All management access requires cryptographic keys
   → SSH Ed25519 keys everywhere
   → Password authentication disabled everywhere

8. DNS queries are encrypted
   → DNS-over-TLS to upstream resolvers
   → ISP cannot observe domain queries
```

### What This Architecture Does Not Guarantee

```
1. Protection if the edge router is physically compromised
   → Physical access to any device breaks the model

2. Protection against ISP-level traffic analysis
   → They can see encrypted traffic volume and timing
   → DNS-over-TLS hides queries but not connection patterns

3. Zero-day exploits in any component
   → Regular updates are required (documented in main guide)

4. Protection if your WireGuard private key is stolen
   → Key rotation procedure is documented

5. Anonymity
   → This is a security architecture, not an anonymity architecture
   → Your public IP is attached to your DuckDNS domain
```

