## Replication Guide

To replicate this architecture on different hardware:

### Step 1 — Choose Your Devices

Fill these four roles with any compatible hardware:

- Edge router running OpenWrt, DD-WRT, or Merlin
- Middle buffer running OpenWrt (64MB RAM minimum)
- Server running Linux with Wi-Fi and Ethernet
- Workstation (Qubes OS recommended, 16GB+ RAM)

### Step 2 — Choose Your Subnets

Pick four non-overlapping subnets and fill in the [variables reference](#variables-reference) at the bottom of this document.

### Step 3 — Follow Build Order

```
1. Configure edge router first
   → WAN working, home DHCP working, WireGuard server up

2. Configure middle router
   → WAN from edge, LAN subnet, hidden SSID, banIP

3. Configure server
   → Connect to hidden SSID as uplink
   → Configure eth0 as Labs gateway
   → nftables kill switch
   → Podman stack

4. Configure ScryptGate
   → Controller board access
   → Local API running
   → Integrated with approval API

5. Configure workstation
   → Connect to Labs switch
   → vault-qube with no network
   → GPU passthrough

6. Verify
   → Run all tests in Section A of the Security Addendum
   → External port scan
   → Kill switch test
   → WireGuard remote access
```

### Step 4 — Harden

Follow the Security Addendum for:

- DNS security
- IDS layer
- Grafana alerting
- Qubes firewall rules

